WEBVTT

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.790
Go fight somewhere else!

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.300
Is this where Ouren-san lives?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.910
She's actually dead. She got sick.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.860
I see. I'm sorry to trouble you.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.310
Are you Tsukishiro-san's friend?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.710
Grandma told me about you.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.930
I'm her granddaughter, Rinko.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.520
I'm guessing the little one is Asahi-chan.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.270
This is my sister.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.020
Well, all right. Come on in.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.940
<b>Book 2: The Snow Continues to Fall</b>

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.750
Make yourselves at home. 
I've already been paid to look after you.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.090
<b>Confidential File 637, A Fleeting Spring</b>

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.090
A real mess, right?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.840
The government took anything 
that was worth much.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.970
Go on, get out of here.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.440
Grandma just kept feeding them.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.810
So cute!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.760
Don't cry to me if it hurts you.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.970
Rub, rub, rub!

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.480
See the building over there? 
That's yours to use.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.680
A white crow? That seems like a bad sign.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.570
Okay, first, I'd better clean up!

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.800
You're tired after such a long trip, right?

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.600
Get some rest.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.310
I'm totally fine! You don't have 
to lift a finger, Onee-chan!

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.760
I'll make sure it's spotless—

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.110
Are you gonna kill it?

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.500
It's not easy to change...

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.510
But I'd like to make the effort.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.160
Who the hell are you?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.830
I don't have to answer to you.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.540
Doesn't matter, anyway! 
I'm not saying anything!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.830
Seiji Todoroki, your foster father is dead.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.430
You killed Dr. Ijichi?!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.680
You have a brother too, don't you?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.930
He's got nothin' to do with this!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:57.440
What's in the notebook that 
Makoto Tsukishiro carries?

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.440
<b>Ichisaki Rice Exchange</b>

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.950
Organically Produced Rice 
<b>Mount Fuji's Shadow</b>

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.950
This is the item we were holding.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.950
<i>Said it was a treasure hunt...</i>

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.700
<i>What kind of treasure?</i>

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.420
<i>Dunno. Supposed to be valuable, though.</i>

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.460
That's the first treasure done.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.340
That leaves three more.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.360
That'll give you enough to 
crush the Tokugawa regime.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:32.850
I'll get rid of the Tokugawas 
and set Yukimura free.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.050
What even is freedom?

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.540
Shut up...

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:41.130
She might be free already, 
without your help.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.230
Shut up!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.930
Shut up already!

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:53.260
Two to go... I swear I'll find them!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.820
We've received reports 
about a suspicious person.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.620
We're going to take a look around.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.780
Go, go!

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.590
All right, here we go...

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.560
There!

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.250
Oh, sorry!

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.540
Hey, it's the girl from the cat temple!

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.260
Come play with us!

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.060
You okay?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.960
Hey! Over here!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.990
Sensei, look!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:56.390
Ladybugs are very sensitive to warmth. 
That's why they always fly toward the light.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.950
Aw, come back!

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.940
Oikawa-sensei.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.150
Thank you for always looking out for her.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.440
It's all right. I enjoy it, too.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.440
There it is!

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:09.950
Sawa-san...

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.550
Yes?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.450
Do you think Asahi-chan 
could start attending classes?

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.240
You two seem to have settled in nicely.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:18.950
That's a good idea.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:24.020
I think Asahi would be happy to have 
you as a teacher, Oikawa-sensei.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.980
Not... yet...

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.400
One left.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.700
<b>Matsumaru Miso Plant</b>

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:05.620
What the...

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:09.210
Karasumori Clan Top Secret Information

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.260
The cherry blossom festival?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.630
It's going to be on the next holiday.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.760
Oikawa-sensei is going!

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.590
I see.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.640
He's pretty hansum, right?

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:21.960
Hansu...?

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:25.040
I think he's a good teacher.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.750
You should come to the festival, then!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.350
No, thank you.

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.650
Yeah, you're coming! It's settled!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.630
I just said that I'm not.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:34.730
What is that?

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.220
Flower pressing!

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:40.250
Oikawa-sensei taught me about it.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.600
If you go like this, 
the flowers will last forever!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.760
Let me see that.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.790
You can't stick so many in together.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:58.570
What is it?

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.850
I'm having fun!

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:04.480
Let's press a bunch of 
different flowers, okay?

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.100
Sure.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.830
<b>Temporarily Closed</b>

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.360
Move!

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.160
What the hell?

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.040
You're in the way!

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.780
Yukimura is dead.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:39.510
The girl who was living 
with her has gone missing.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.260
I'm sure you were involved, Tsukishiro.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.400
Are you going to kill me?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.770
You look like you only have 
three days left, anyway.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.770
Painkillers. The doctor told me everything.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.940
If you want them, hand it over.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.050
You want to see Yukimura again 
before dying, don't you?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.810
You just said she was dead...

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.950
I'm just humoring their farce.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.090
That's in poor taste.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:07.190
I know where to find them.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.460
If you hand that bag over, 
I'll leave Yukimura alone.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.860
And that's all of it?

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:23.260
Do you want me to strip so you can check?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.270
That won't be necessary.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.960
Pity, from you? How uncharacteristic.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.270
Did you find the treasurer's treasures?

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.760
I'm going to take Yukimura from you.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.810
Not a flicker of caution...

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.700
Tsuki-san?

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.390
Thank you so much.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.880
You managed to do it.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.980
It's warm.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:38.040
When I reach out from my futon 
at night, she's always there.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.670
And it's so warm.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.430
Warmth is precious 
because of how fleeting it is.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.820
She killed your parents.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.500
Not just yours.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.940
She's killed more people 
than you can imagine.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.200
There's no way she can change.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.000
She... can't... change...

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.690
Are you okay? Does it hurt?

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.060
Damn it!

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.770
She hasn't completed her revenge...

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.330
But she...

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:15.110
I need to tell Yukimura the truth.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.550
Yukimura is dead!

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.260
Please. Don't wake her.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:32.310
I should've killed you after all.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.310
Asahi-chan?

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:40.810
Onee-chan?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.580
This is a hand-me-down, but I thought 
it'd look good on Sawa-chan.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.500
I've got one for you too, Asahi-chan.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.490
I don't think I should go after all.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.130
Quit moving!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.260
Right...

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.380
If you keep pouting like that, 
you're never going to find a husband!

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:16.140
I don't plan on getting married.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.800
This festival is gonna be fun!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.810
Was the festival canceled?

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.770
Did something happen?

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:31.660
The Ryumyaku supply has been unstable, 
so the idea is to cut down on it.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.090
The village office is having trouble, too.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.660
I was really looking forward to it...

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:38.820
Well...

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.420
So pretty!

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.180
This is the best I can manage.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.050
Oh, I forgot something!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.490
What is it?

00:13:58.490 --> 00:13:59.940
I'll go get it!

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.840
I should go with you. It's dangerous.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.420
Oh, it's fine!

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.220
But...

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.650
Oh, I should let you know!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.020
You're really cute when 
you smile, Onee-chan!

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:17.120
Sensei! Look after my sister, okay?

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.780
What were you talking about?

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.080
Something silly.

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:27.950
It's been so long since 
I took in the cherry blossoms.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.400
Were you busy in Tokyo?

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.410
No...

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.180
I stayed there for a while, 
when I was a student.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.230
Where did you live?

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.200
Ryumyaku...

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:47.860
Is the Ryumyaku supply being unstable 
something that happens often?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:52.740
The majority of Ryumyaku gets sent to Tokyo, 
despite where it's originally mined.

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:54.410
Is that the reason why?

00:14:55.450 --> 00:15:00.010
One of the village's Ryumyaku 
wells dried up this year.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.920
I hope she's doing a good job.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.170
Oh, Nana, are you jealous?

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:11.990
Want me to rub your head?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:19.520
I know. I'll tell her about Tsuki-san.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:25.520
But still, y'know... 
I want her to have fun today.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:29.070
Our country is able to stand on 
even footing with foreign countries

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.990
because we have Ryumyaku, 
which doesn't exist anywhere else.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:38.030
It's used in everything... fuel, 
electricity, even metal processing.

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.500
That's why everyone's scared.

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:42.750
Things are quiet enough around here,

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:46.760
but in the cities, things 
are getting really heated.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:53.040
Don't you think things have gotten crazy since
 what happened with Satsuma and Choshu?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.260
I'm not sure.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.450
The real issue is that they try 
to suppress dissent with violence.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.140
Not even being open to discussion...

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.770
It's like they're animals! No, worse!

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.630
Oh, sorry, I got carried away.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:10.820
It's fine.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.780
I guess it's a pretty boring subject.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.560
It's not... boring.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.810
The wind's starting to pick up.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:29.670
Tsuki?

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.390
A friend of yours?

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.510
Excuse me for a moment.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.510
You've become a real bore.

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.400
Didn't you help make this happen?

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.940
You gave Asahi the medicine 
and told me about this place.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:48.980
We can talk later. For now, you need to run.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.940
I'm not going anywhere.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:57.370
I idolized you.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.950
The way you were so desperate to survive, 
even with the world against you, was beautiful.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.960
You were weak, but strong. 
Fragile, but enduring.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:07.740
It was a beauty unique to you.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.960
But now... you have none of that.

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.720
Sawa-chan?

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.050
This is a lie!

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:19.630
Please...

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:22.180
Does he even know the real you?!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.390
Stop it.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.640
What about your revenge?!

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.140
Stop it!

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.700
She's clearly upset. Let her go.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:31.780
Let go.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.490
You're not going to ask?

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.660
You don't want to talk about it, right?

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.080
But...

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:18.910
If it's a burden, one causing you pain, 
then I'd like to help you.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:28.500
Sensei?

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.230
Sensei?! Sensei!

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.770
No!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:40.880
Asahi?!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:47.620
Asahi!

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.770
Onee-chan, stay back!

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.160
Tsuki?

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.170
Oh, this is such a relief!

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:13.000
Why?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.800
Tsuki, how could you?

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:21.640
The drugs the snake left behind are fantastic!

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.610
I'm back from the brink 
of death, thanks to them!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.120
Don't!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.740
I'll be finished before you can start.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.560
If you want to kill someone, kill me.

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.510
You can't die yet.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:40.720
What do you want? Why would you do this?

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:43.570
I want Yukimura back.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:48.080
Onee-chan isn't Yukimura anymore!

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:49.620
Asahi...

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:54.670
I sincerely just want to help you, Yukimura.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:57.340
I want to make your revenge a reality.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.500
That's never changed.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:03.440
And I'll get rid of anything 
that's in the way!

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.680
I won't let you!

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:09.470
Onee-chan, no!

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.140
Asahi!

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:29.680
No...

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:33.600
Asahi?

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:37.000
Asahi! Asahi!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.150
No...

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:43.550
No!

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:50.980
Why? Why?

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.620
Asahi...

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.890
...pay...

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.490
You will pay.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.480
You, who would violate the 
foundation of what makes a man,

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:14.620
dwell now in the blue that surges within!

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.150
Welcome back, Yukimura.
